{"resourceIdentifier":"3996","resourceName":"Family Forest Carbon Program - Central Appalachia","description":"The Family Forest Carbon Program (FFCP), administered by the Family Forest Impact Foundation (FFIF), is an innovative, incentive-based program engaging private family and other non-industrial private forest landowners throughout the United States in improved forest management practices, promoting forest health, carbon sequestration and storage, and other environmental conservation and protection practices. \r\n\r\nThrough its grouped project design, the FFCP is able to engage and achieve economies of scale with smaller non-industrial forestland owners, reaching ownerships that have been largely unrepresented in voluntary carbon markets. The FFCP solves challenges to small forest holdings participation in carbon projects, by reducing cost and complexity of participation. \r\n\r\nFFCP provides incentive payments to forest landowners to implement climate-smart practices that increase sequestration and storage of carbon. The FFCP further connects enrolled landowners with technical assistance from local consulting foresters, helping family landowners transition to long-term, sustainable forest management. \r\n\r\nThe first project activities implemented in the FFCP program (directed towards the U.S. Central Appalachia region) include: Growing Mature Forests (GMF) –20-year, renewable agreement to limit timber harvest (with imposition of minimum residual basal area and riparian buffers and prohibition on high-grading/diameter limit cuts), thereby increasing net growth. The GMF practice, compared to common practice high-grading in the region, is expected to generate net emission reductions of ~1.6 t CO2e/acre/year. total GHG emission reductions and removals.\r\n\r\nThe project activity instance locations of this project disclosed in the public kml file correspond to the centroids of the counties where the project's activities are located. Specific details of the project activities’ locations can be requested at datarequest@forestfoundation.org","location":{"latitude":40.267268,"longitude":-78.313505},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-08-31","endExclusive":"2023-10-01","endInclusive":"2023-09-30"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3996"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"PA"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Family Forest Impact Foundation"},{"type":"string","value":"DC, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"703.344.4918"},{"type":"string","value":"lriley@familyforestimpact.org"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3996"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3996"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"231124"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":3929}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"IFM"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0045"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"13929 Acres"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Aster Global Environmental Solutions Inc."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"20/11/2025"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 06/07/2021 - 05/07/2041"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=81954&IDKEY=fkjalskjf098234kj28098sfkjlf098098kl32lasjdflkj909l113014566","doc